jeregrette-by-fitandbandwagon for Debian
---------------------------------------

The orig tarball contains the source release of the intro, published on
http://ftp.kameli.net/pub/fit/je_regrette/ : main.c, osa.c, syna.c,
syna.h, biisi.c (the music), letters2.h, Makefile and README.txt.
osa.c and the Makefile were reformatted with uncrustify in 2019.

Patches (debian/patches):
 01  Makefile using pkg-config and the dpkg-buildflags (CPPFLAGS, CFLAGS,
     LDFLAGS), with an install target
 02  clear the echo buffers of the synthesizer
 03  fix compiler warnings
 04  port from SDL 1.2 to SDL2
 05  quit with Escape, Q or the window close button
 06  toggle fullscreen with the F key
 07  64-bit portability warnings
 08  enable V-Sync, let SDL convert the audio format (the synthesizer only
     writes signed 16-bit stereo samples), sleep instead of spinning when
     the 100 Hz limiter skips a frame, fix the -w option
 09  linear filtering of the feedback textures: with GL_NEAREST the motion
     blur drew a line at exactly half the height of the image

Written by Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>, reviewed by Nicolas HOUDELOT.

